Do not record a folded bytecode result as a CSE expression.

The ARM code generator folds imul and iadd into mla and skips the iadd.
CSE recorded that result for the bytes up to imul, which push two values.
A later match pushed one value, so the following iadd consumed the last
local and shifted the stack for later invocations.

--- a/cldc/src/vm/share/compiler/BytecodeCompileClosure.cpp
+++ b/cldc/src/vm/share/compiler/BytecodeCompileClosure.cpp
@@ -2344,7 +2344,14 @@
               "Invalid expression start bci");
     GUARANTEE(!raw_location->is_two_word(), "2-word expressions not supported");
     if (raw_location->in_register()) {
-      const int next_bci = method()->next_bci(current_bci);
+      const int bytecode_end = method()->next_bci(current_bci);
+      if (bytecode_end != next_bci) {
+        // The code generator folded the following bytecodes into this one,
+        // such as imul and iadd into mla. The bytes of this expression no
+        // longer push the register value, so CSE must not reuse it.
+        vsf->clear_expression(raw_location->get_register());
+        return;
+      }

       ExpressionAttributeClosure cl;
       cl.initialize(method());
